  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Six mill posts write the G84 F word with the exact tap feed: `fanuc`, `doosan-dnm`, `mazak`, `sinumerik`, `tormach`, `linuxcnc`.\n- The F word has three decimals in mm/min and four decimals in in/min. Trailing zeros are removed.\n- The Fanuc-family posts (`fanuc`, `doosan-dnm`, `mazak`) keep the point on a whole tap feed (`F750.`). This follows their own length-word rule (#1836). `sinumerik`, `tormach` and `linuxcnc` write `F750`.\n- Each post checks the pitch that the control reads (written F / written S) against the stream pitch (feed / rpm). A difference of more than 0.01 percent refuses the tap by name, with the operation name. No G84 is written then.\n- The F words of other moves do not change. #3690 owns those.\n- The approach and the tolerance are the same as the Mach4 fix (#3701, PR #3731).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/3699-tap-feed-precision.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach post wrote the G84 feed with `ff()`, which rounds a mm feed to a whole number (`Math.round`) and an inch feed to two decimals. The stream keeps the tap feed at 0.001 mm/min. M1.4 x 0.3 at S115 needs F34.5. The posts wrote `F35`, and the control cut a pitch that is 1.45 percent too long.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New pin: `crates/post/tests/tap_feed_mill_posts.rs`, one test for each post:\n  - `fanuc_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed`\n  - `doosan_dnm_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed`\n  - `mazak_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed`\n  - `sinumerik_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed`\n  - `tormach_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed`\n  - `linuxcnc_g84_keeps_exact_tap_feed` (floating tap, which is G84 on LinuxCNC)\n- Each test pins: F34.5 at S115 and F133.2 at S333 (the two feeds of the issue), F34.561 (three decimals), a whole feed (`F600.` or `F600`), inch F1.3583 and F5.2441, a refusal for S115.4 (the S word changes the pitch), and a refusal for an inch feed below the smallest step.\n- Red before the fix: all 6 tests failed on upstream/main fe385c642 (`left: Some(\"F35\")`, `right: Some(\"F34.5\")`).\n- Mutation 1: I removed only the `tapPitchHolds` call in all six posts. All 6 tests failed at the refusal assert. Restored: green.\n- Mutation 2: I put back only `fw(p.FeedRate)` for the G84 word in all six posts. All 6 tests failed (`F35`). Restored: green.\n- `mach4` already has a three-decimal pin (`F34.561` in `mach4_feed_decimals.rs`, PR #3731). This PR does not change it.\n- New top-level test file: `crates/post/tests/` has no directory test suite (its directories are support modules only). The binary is small and runs in milliseconds.\n\n## Gate (on upstream/main fe385c642)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 796 steps, 2 failed. Both failures came from this change, and I fixed them:\n  - `fanuc_rigid_tap_m29_without_spindle_speed_is_refused_by_name`: the new pitch check ran before the M29 refusal. The M29 refusal now runs first.\n  - `tormach_explains_every_conformance_golden_without_changing_the_program`: the explain golden had the old inch tap feed. I regenerated it (see Goldens moved).\n- After the two fixes, on the final head:\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (all 140 binaries): green.\n  - `app suites: conformance`: 7 passed.\n  - `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: green. No recorded program changed.\n  - Targeted heavy step (P1 rule): `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: example_catalog\"`: 1 step, ok (115 s).\n  - `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 4 steps, 0 failed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- I did not run the full 796-step quick plan again after the two fixes. The second change touched only `fanuc.cps` (the order of two refusals) and one golden. All `camcraft-post` suites and the app suites that read the post goldens ran again.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n`app suites: conformance` and `post suites: explain_tormach` (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`). Eight programs changed, each on its G84 line only:\n\n| Program | Before | After | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `nc/tap_plate.nc` (fanuc) | `F750` | `F750.` | Fanuc-family point on the tap F |\n| `nc/doosan-dnm/tap_plate.nc` | `F750` | `F750.` | same |\n| `nc/mazak/tap_plate.nc` | `F750` | `F750.` | same |\n| `nc/synth_fanuc.nc` | `F240` | `F240.` | same |\n| `nc/synth_doosan-dnm.nc` | `F240` | `F240.` | same |\n| `nc/synth_mazak.nc` | `F240` | `F240.` | same |\n| `nc/tormach/tap_plate.nc` (inch) | `F29.53` | `F29.5276` | 750 / 25.4 at four decimals |\n| `nc/tormach/explain_tap_plate.nc` (inch) | `F29.53 (... FEED RATE 29.53)` | `F29.5276 (... FEED RATE 29.5276)` | same |\n\nNo other line changed. The sinumerik and linuxcnc goldens have whole metric tap feeds, so they do not change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a real control.\n- A Fanuc, Doosan or Mazak control that rejects a decimal point in an F word is not known. The point reads the same at DPI=0 and DPI=1.\n- The general F form of other moves (#3690) is not changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these six post scripts.\n\nThe v0.26.0 cut is in progress. This PR is a draft; it does not merge until after the tag.\n\nChangelog: The fanuc, doosan-dnm, mazak, sinumerik, tormach and linuxcnc posts write the exact G84 tap feed (for example F34.5, not F35) and refuse a tap whose written F and S change the pitch.\n\nFixes #3699\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
